course: dictionary
lesson: 1157
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as separate senses, and context tells you which one the writer means. Brine is one of these words. Its main meaning is very salty water.
explain: «Sea monkeys» are brine shrimps that live in very salty lakes where fish cannot live. The clues are salty and no fish, so brine means very salty water here. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: In cooking, brine is salty water used to keep food fresh or add flavour, such as for pickles or olives. You can also use brine as a verb: to brine food is to soak it in brine. In stories, «the brine» can mean the sea, so look at the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: «Brine» means very salty water.
fact: «Brine» can also mean salty water used to keep food fresh or add flavour, such as for pickles or olives.
fact: In stories, «the brine» can mean the sea.
fact: Brine can be a verb: food is brined when it is soaked in salty water.
fact: Flamingos are pink from the colours in the algae and brine shrimp they eat.
exercise: In science, Sam evaporates brine to get salt crystals. What is brine? | A type of sand | Fresh rain water | *Very salty water | A fizzy drink
exercise: The children sat on the cliff and watched the brine roll in. What does brine mean here? | A petrol station | *The sea | A pickle jar | A bird's nest
exercise: Mum uses brine to keep the olives fresh. Find and copy the word that means salty water. | Mum | olives | fresh | *brine
test: «Sea monkeys» live in very salty lakes where fish cannot live. Which clue tells you what brine means? | *Very salty lakes where fish cannot live | Flamingos eat them | Sea monkeys | Brine shrimps are small
test: Ben says brine must be a sea creature because of brine shrimp. Is he right? | Yes, brine shrimp and brine are the same thing | *No, brine is salty water, and brine shrimp live in it | Yes, brine is a kind of shrimp | No, brine is a bird
exam: What does it mean to brine the chicken before cooking it? | To cut it into small pieces | *To soak it in salty water | To freeze it solid | To paint it bright pink
